saturday marked the fourth summit of the  community of latin american and  caribbean states or select and this  year's international dialogue held in  mexico city was full of surprises  starting with the unexpected appearance  of venezuela's nicolas maduro who  arrived unannounced overnight  the visit placed maduro across the table  from other leftist leaders at a summit  that excludes the participation of the  united states  we have enough stones to throw at some  of you but we didn't come here to throw  stones we came to extend our hand and  work together  not everyone at the 2021 selak summit  was welcoming of the venezuelan  delegation  my presence at this summit in no way  represents a recognition of the  government of mr nicolas maduro  my government has not changed its  position and i believe it's between  gentlemen to say this face to face  another unexpected appearance was  chinese president xi jinping who sent a  pre-recorded message promising more  cooperation between china and latin  america  the ties between china and latin america  have entered a new era characterized by  equality mutual benefit innovation and  well-being of the people  nearly 20 heads of state participated in  the summit including cuba's miguel  diaz-canel the cuban leader called for  an end to u.s sanctions and was among  many who criticized the organization of  american states calling the oas a tool  of u.s interests  it is the oas at the service of the  united states that has supported  attempts to isolate cuba military  interventions in latin america and the  caribbean government overthrows and  military dictatorships  host mexican president andres manuel  lopez obrador went further saying latin  american and caribbean nations should  aspire to form a regional bloc similar  to the european union  in these times silac can become the  principal instrument to consolidate  relations between our latin american and  caribbean nations  [Music]  despite moments of contention there was  also agreement among select members  including building on a regional  strategy to face the challenges of the  coronavirus pandemic  and establishing a regional fund to  serve as relief during natural disasters  linked to climate change  the 2021 cell act conference is seen by  many as an opportunity for mexico to  position itself as a power player and a  regional mediator working toward  restoring multilateralism and ending the  diplomatic rift that exists between the  united states and leftist latin american  countries like cuba and venezuela manuel  rapalo al jazeera mexico city
 

